    "text": "In a world where the skies are stitched with dreams,  \nA traveler’s path is woven with gleams.  \nThrough the mist of a morning, they gleam,  \nA journey that’s both swift and serene.  \n\nThe wind whispers tales of distant lands,  \nWhere the stars are stitched in a quiet hands.  \nEach step is a thread, each mile a thread,  \nA tapestry of the soul, so red.  \n\nThe map is a thread, the road a thread,  \nA dance of the heart, a rhythm so red.  \nWith every stitch, a story is told,  \nA tale of the soul, a tale of the sold.  \n\nThe traveler’s heart is a loom, a loom,  \nA loom of the soul, a loom of the home.  \nWith every thread, a journey is born,  \nA journey that’s both swift and serene.  \n\nSo here’s to the trips that we take,  \nAnd the stitches that bind us to the place.  \nFor in every thread, a story is told,  \nA tale of the soul, a tale of the sold.",
